WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.801
- All these false stories.

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.036
This kid comes from a family

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.038
with family members
of multiple races.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:08.041
They did a deep dive on
all of his social media.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:11.611
They did a colonoscopic kind
of review of his social media

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.346
and they found no connections

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.815 align:start size:84% position:16%
to any form of
racism of any kind,

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:18.385 align:start size:84% position:16%
no connections to
militia of any kind,

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:20.987
no connections to anybody
like that of any kind,

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.656
no statements like
that at any time.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.793
All they had was that he had
once gone to a Trump rally.

00:00:26.793 --> 00:00:28.428
That was their sole basis,

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:30.296
the, "Oh, you went
to a Trump rally,"

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.531 align:start size:84% position:16%
and like most-
- Well, there you go.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.134 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Exactly, and he's
a gun supporter

00:00:34.134 --> 00:00:36.770
and he's a police,
military supporter,

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.972
and that was it, but
all they just did,

00:00:38.972 --> 00:00:41.174
most of the media ran with
these false allegations,

00:00:41.174 --> 00:00:42.675
these stream of false,

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:45.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
to this day, they continue
to tell false stories,

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:47.680 align:start size:88% position:13%
the prosecutors continue
to lie about 'em

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.717
using court proceedings
to get away with the lie.

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:53.420 align:start position:0%
The kid's the most innocent
defendant I've ever represented,

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.689
ever been involved with, but
the case goes far past him.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:01:00.093 align:start position:0%
If he gets convicted,
self-defense is dead in America.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.595
(gentle music)

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.136 line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin and joining
me today is a trial lawyer

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.939 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
and an all-star
political gambler,

00:01:12.939 --> 00:01:16.643 align:start size:84% position:16%
also a primo promoter
of locals.com.

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:19.179 align:start size:97% position:3%
Robert Barnes, welcome
back to "The Rubin Report."

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.447
- Glad to be here.

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:21.915
- I am glad to have you, man.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.517
I didn't realize until
literally two minutes ago

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:28.822
that we have not spoken
in a one-on-one forum

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.490
for over two years.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.961
Is the world getting better
or worse in those two years?

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:37.997 line:0%
- Back then, I was taking a
lot of controversial cases.

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.333 line:0%
We were talking about Alex
Jones, the Covington kids,

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:43.002 line:0%
Wesley Snipes, Ralph
Nader, Girls Gone Wild,

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:44.537
all the rest of it,

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I decided to take
less controversial cases,

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:48.241
so I took Donald Trump

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.143 align:start size:84% position:16%
(Dave laughing)
during the elections,

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.778
Amy Cooper in New York,

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.646
Kyle Rittenhouse, self-defense,

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:55.415
but yeah, the world just
keeps getting crazier,

00:01:55.415 --> 00:01:57.817
particularly from a legal
political perspective.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:59.986 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, so what
put you on the map?

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:02.222
Is it fair to say that what
originally put you on the map

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:04.457 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a bigger sense
was the bet on Trump?

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.659
Is that really the thing
that got you out there

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.428
as more of a public lawyer?

00:02:08.428 --> 00:02:09.662
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:11.631
Basically, I'd always
done a lot of tax work,

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:12.866
but for a lot of reasons,

00:02:12.866 --> 00:02:14.801
I didn't need that
to be high profile,

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.202
and I'd done a lot
of civil rights work

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:18.771 align:start size:88% position:13%
but had not made
myself a public figure,

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.141 align:start size:84% position:16%
but people had
followed the Trump bet

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.742 align:start size:84% position:16%
because it was a big
bet and the rest,

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:24.043
became a public figure,

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.445 align:start size:81% position:19%
and during the
Trump time period,

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:28.581 align:start size:88% position:13%
it became more important
to be a public figure

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.151
defending certain issues in
the court of public opinion.

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:33.720
- Yeah, and now you're
an all-star YouTuber

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:35.555
who hangs out like this all day,

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:38.024 align:start size:88% position:13%
(Robert laughing)
like world, come at me.

00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:39.526
I want to get into
some of those cases

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:41.127
that you've covered, obviously,

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:44.531
but let's start with
Trump's current lawsuit

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:46.900
because just in the
last 10 days or so,

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:50.837 align:start size:97% position:3%
he has announced that he's
basically going after Big Tech

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:53.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a class action lawsuit,
and not just Big Tech,

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:56.075
but actually some of the
heads of these companies.

00:02:56.075 --> 00:02:58.178
Can you give people the 101,

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.980
the sort of must have info on
what the lawsuit actually is,

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.783 align:start size:97% position:3%
and then we'll talk about
the chances of it succeeding?

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:06.219
- Sure, so basically, Trump
has brought a claim saying

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:08.621 align:start size:84% position:16%
that all the Big
Tech giants conspired

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.790
with various government actors

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.926 align:start size:81% position:19%
to kick him off
of and exclude him

00:03:12.926 --> 00:03:14.394
from all of their platforms,

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:17.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he is saying that they
did so as state actors

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.133 align:start size:97% position:3%
and thus are subject to
First Amendment limitations.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.135
That's the core of his
claim against Google,

00:03:22.135 --> 00:03:24.003 align:start size:84% position:16%
against Facebook
and against Twitter,

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.972
as well as Dorsey, Zuckerberg,

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:28.208
and the Google CEO individually.

00:03:28.208 --> 00:03:29.742
- The key there seems
to be some kind of

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.177
collusion with the government.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:34.013 align:start position:0%
He's not arguing just that
Twitter, Facebook and Instagram

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.448 align:start size:84% position:16%
all sat down and
maybe did something,

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:37.350 align:start size:97% position:3%
but somehow there was a
connection to the government.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:40.153
Do you have any idea if
there's evidence of that

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:44.524
or what he could actually
prove that would show it?

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:47.260
- I think they may, in
an amended complaint,

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.662 align:start size:84% position:16%
make better
allegations factually,

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:51.864
but there's inferential evidence

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.567
that Fauci, Pelosi and Harris

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
had specifically requested
each of those platforms

00:03:57.770 --> 00:03:59.973 align:start size:84% position:16%
to remove Trump from
those platforms.

00:03:59.973 --> 00:04:02.408
Some of that's based on some
of their public statements.

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:04.911
Some of that's based on some
of the emails that came out

00:04:04.911 --> 00:04:07.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the FOIA request
with Fauci and Zuckerberg.

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.182
There was much more collusion.

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:11.150 align:start size:84% position:16%
Some of that is
indirectly referenced

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.353
by Robert Kennedy's
suit against Facebook

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:16.789
pending in California about
the same set of allegations.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:19.192
I think if they make
better allegations,

00:04:19.192 --> 00:04:22.729
they may be able to get to the
discovery stage and find out

00:04:22.729 --> 00:04:25.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
just how much these Big
Tech giants were operating

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:28.067
at the direct request
of government actors.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.535
- Before we get to discovery,

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.137
which obviously is the
interesting part of this,

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:33.439
why is he doing it
as a class action

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:36.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
and not just him going
after them for how he was,

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:41.114
in his eyes, basically wronged.

00:04:41.114 --> 00:04:42.482
- I think his purpose in this,

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.150
his heart is in the right place.

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:45.918
I think some of the
lawyers involved

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:49.255
might not have the technical
skill to translate that well

00:04:49.255 --> 00:04:51.924 align:start size:97% position:3%
because there could've been
a class action alleging

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:56.062
that Big Tech is really part
of the public digital square

00:04:56.062 --> 00:04:57.463 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the public
square has just moved

00:04:57.463 --> 00:04:59.532
from the physical world
to the digital world

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:01.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
and from the geographic
world to the online world,

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.903 align:start size:97% position:3%
and he would have had, I
think, a strong claim on that,

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:06.472 align:start size:97% position:3%
at least to challenge
existing law and to extend it.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:08.274
They didn't really do that.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:11.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
This particular class
action isn't the strongest

00:05:11.577 --> 00:05:13.012
because what he's
alleging, really,

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:16.082 align:start size:97% position:3%
is that he was targeted
because he was President Trump

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:17.917
and he's trying to bring
all these other people in

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:20.186
that had been targeted
for political reasons,

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.754
but they're not President Trump.

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.389
From a pure legal perspective,

00:05:23.389 --> 00:05:25.558
technically it's
not the best claim.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:27.794
- Can you explain just
how the process works?

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:30.129
He now brings this class action

00:05:30.129 --> 00:05:33.066
and how does it
get to the judge,

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:35.568
and is it one judge
that will decide

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.937
if this thing can go to trial?

00:05:37.937 --> 00:05:40.139 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Effectively, here's
what's likely to happen.

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:42.008
They'll likely try to
move to transfer it

00:05:42.008 --> 00:05:44.210
from the Southern District of
Florida, where he filed it,

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.379 align:start size:84% position:16%
to the Northern
District of California

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.614
on grounds that it's a
term of service dispute,

00:05:48.614 --> 00:05:50.016
at least Twitter.

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:53.052 align:start size:97% position:3%
Probably Facebook and YouTube
will try that as well.

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:54.587
That will be his first fight-

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:55.755
- Meaning you get it to Cali

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:57.290 align:start size:84% position:16%
'cause that's where
they're based.

00:05:57.290 --> 00:06:00.760
- Exactly, and they have some
contractual language that can,

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:03.796
depending on the nature of
the claim, require that.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:05.965
They're gonna want

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:07.834
a different district
court judge assigned

00:06:07.834 --> 00:06:09.268
and a different
court of appeals.

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:11.704 align:start position:0%
They'll want the Ninth Circuit,
not the Eleventh Circuit.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:14.307 align:start size:88% position:13%
They'll also want
anti-SLAPP law to apply,

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:15.808
which doesn't apply in Florida,

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.777 align:start size:81% position:19%
but it would apply
in California,

00:06:17.777 --> 00:06:19.479 align:start size:84% position:16%
because that would
make Trump responsible

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:22.482
for the other side's
legal fees if he loses.

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:23.850
That will be his
first big battle.

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:26.085
The second battle would
be a motion to dismiss

00:06:26.085 --> 00:06:28.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
before it ever gets to
class certification stage.

00:06:28.888 --> 00:06:32.191
If he wins at that level,
then he gets discovery,

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.459
and then after that,

00:06:33.459 --> 00:06:35.695
a single judge usually
decides whether or not

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:37.530
there's class certification.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.533
He's got several procedural
hurdles to get through first.

00:06:40.533 --> 00:06:41.801
- Who decides that part?

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:43.669
Because it seems to
me that this thing,

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:47.473
even if Trump doesn't win, if
it at least gets to discovery,

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:49.709
we're gonna find out something.

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:51.244 align:start size:84% position:16%
If Twitter and
Facebook and YouTube

00:06:51.244 --> 00:06:53.780 align:start size:84% position:16%
have to open up the
books and really show,

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:58.151
oh, members of Congress or the
Senate or the administration

00:06:58.151 --> 00:07:01.254 align:start position:0%
were actually DMing people,
coordinating some of this stuff,

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:02.288
or whatever else it's showing

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:04.657 align:start size:88% position:13%
related to
manipulating algorithms

00:07:04.657 --> 00:07:06.125
or shadow banning
or anything else,

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:08.928 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's like that's the win,
even if it's not a legal win.

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:11.063
How do we at least get there?

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:13.699
- Basically, he needs to
enhance the complaint.

00:07:13.699 --> 00:07:15.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he should add
some lawyers to the team,

00:07:15.668 --> 00:07:18.271
like Alan Dershowitz,
like Harmeet Dhillon.

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:19.472
Harmeet Dhillon has a very good

00:07:19.472 --> 00:07:21.808 align:start size:88% position:13%
state action Twitter
claim currently pending,

00:07:21.808 --> 00:07:25.578
so add some lawyers who are
familiar with this space

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:26.813
and change his complaint.

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:29.081
His complaint as
it currently exists

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.217
won't get him past
a motion to dismiss,

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:32.485
but if they add to it,

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:34.987
I think he has good
grounds to allege

00:07:34.987 --> 00:07:37.290
that these individual
actors were acting

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:41.160 align:start size:97% position:3%
at the direct request of
Vice President Kamala Harris

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.095
and of speaker of the
House, Nancy Pelosi,

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:45.765 align:start size:88% position:13%
and maybe of Anthony
Fauci in other contexts,

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:47.633
and then I think he
can get to discovery,

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.035
and you're absolutely right.

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:52.038
There's gonna be a lot
of revelatory discovery

00:07:52.038 --> 00:07:53.673
if he can get to that stage.

00:07:53.673 --> 00:07:55.675
I hope he improves the case

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:57.677 align:start size:81% position:19%
so that he can
get to that stage.

00:07:57.677 --> 00:07:59.612
- I sense you think
maybe he doesn't have

00:07:59.612 --> 00:08:01.848 align:start size:97% position:3%
the best legal representatives
around him right now,

00:08:01.848 --> 00:08:03.416
the way you're describing it.

00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:04.684
- No.

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:06.686
It's one of these groups
that's a DC-based group,

00:08:06.686 --> 00:08:09.655
that their roots are in big
oil, corporate lobbying.

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:13.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you wanted a regulatory
issue on energy,

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.161
they're fantastic.

00:08:15.161 --> 00:08:17.563 align:start size:97% position:3%
First Amendment constitutional
issue on Big Tech,

00:08:17.563 --> 00:08:19.732 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's not their
area or focal point.

00:08:19.732 --> 00:08:22.635
I think these lawyers are
lawyers that are unfamiliar

00:08:22.635 --> 00:08:25.004
with this space and it
showed up in the suit,

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:27.740 align:start position:0%
and right now, those of us
that are familiar in this space

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:29.976 align:start size:84% position:16%
that want this lawsuit
to move forward

00:08:29.976 --> 00:08:33.012
are very concerned that, as
alleged, this lawsuit is DOA.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.681
He can improve it though.

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:38.351
He's got plenty of times to
amend it, but with Trump,

00:08:38.351 --> 00:08:41.587 align:start size:97% position:3%
sometimes his personnel picks
are a little hit or miss.

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:43.589 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Did you think about picking
up the phone and saying,

00:08:43.589 --> 00:08:45.591 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Hey, guys, I know a little
something about this.

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:47.226
We have some connections here"?

00:08:47.226 --> 00:08:48.394
- Actually, a bunch of us did,

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:51.564
and it's just Trump is Trump.

00:08:51.564 --> 00:08:53.666 align:start size:84% position:16%
He makes his decisions
at different times.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:57.203
I've been telling him ever
since, actually, November

00:08:57.203 --> 00:08:59.138
that he should be on Locals.

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:00.306 align:start size:84% position:16%
(Dave laughing)
If you want to compete

00:09:00.306 --> 00:09:01.908
with all the Big Tech people,

00:09:01.908 --> 00:09:04.243 align:start size:88% position:13%
what better way to
monetize Trump's brand?

00:09:04.243 --> 00:09:06.479
There's so many different
ways he could do this,

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:08.548 align:start size:97% position:3%
but he has a lot of other
people whispering in his ear,

00:09:08.548 --> 00:09:09.982
and I think some of the people

00:09:09.982 --> 00:09:11.217
that are whispering in his ear

00:09:11.217 --> 00:09:13.252
don't really want him
to succeed in his suit,

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.155 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it was a problem
throughout his four years,

00:09:16.155 --> 00:09:19.091
that there was an angel on
one side, on one shoulder,

00:09:19.091 --> 00:09:20.359
a devil on the other

00:09:20.359 --> 00:09:22.562
and he doesn't always
get the best advice,

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:24.397 align:start size:84% position:16%
but people are
telling him that now.

00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:26.098
I hope he takes
corrective action

00:09:26.098 --> 00:09:27.667 align:start size:81% position:19%
before the case
can get dismissed.

00:09:27.667 --> 00:09:30.269
- For the record, I know
you're not the only person

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:31.804
in somewhat of the inner circle

00:09:31.804 --> 00:09:33.639
that has mentioned Locals
to him, and the truth is,

00:09:33.639 --> 00:09:35.841
although it would cause us
some headaches, obviously,

00:09:35.841 --> 00:09:38.077
and there would be
some legal issues

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:40.179
and technical stuff
and all of that,

00:09:40.179 --> 00:09:41.614
he of course is
welcome on there,

00:09:41.614 --> 00:09:42.949
and I honestly think
the guy could make

00:09:42.949 --> 00:09:44.784
probably 250 million a month

00:09:44.784 --> 00:09:46.385
on the idea that
50 million people

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:47.920 align:start size:84% position:16%
would give him
probably five bucks

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.121
to be part of that community.

00:09:49.121 --> 00:09:52.558 align:start size:84% position:16%
It's bananas, but
he's doing his thing.

00:09:52.558 --> 00:09:54.160
- It's the best way
to take out Big Tech.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:55.695 align:start size:84% position:16%
The best way to really
take out Big Tech

00:09:55.695 --> 00:09:57.296
is to replace Big Tech,

00:09:57.296 --> 00:10:00.600 align:start size:97% position:3%
and I think his heart is
absolutely in the right place

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:01.534
in bringing this suit,

00:10:01.534 --> 00:10:03.102 line:0%
credit to him for doing so.

00:10:03.102 --> 00:10:05.171 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
It doesn't translate
as well legally,

00:10:05.171 --> 00:10:07.139 align:start size:84% position:16% line:0%
but it's another
place where he could

00:10:07.139 --> 00:10:08.874 line:0%
mount a better challenge

00:10:08.874 --> 00:10:12.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
if he's also supporting
independent tech platforms

00:10:12.378 --> 00:10:15.014 align:start size:88% position:13%
that are the real threat
to Big Tech longterm.

00:10:15.014 --> 00:10:16.282 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I know we've discussed
this a little bit,

00:10:16.282 --> 00:10:17.683
but I'm curious, in
the last two years,

00:10:17.683 --> 00:10:18.951
if you've shifted at all.

00:10:18.951 --> 00:10:21.287
Where are you on in
terms of regulation

00:10:21.287 --> 00:10:23.823
or breaking 'em up or nothing

00:10:23.823 --> 00:10:25.725
or something that
I'm not mentioning?

00:10:25.725 --> 00:10:27.960
- Interestingly enough,
Senator Rubio has put,

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:30.930 align:start position:0%
it was a bill I proposed to
Senator Hawley three years ago.

00:10:30.930 --> 00:10:33.299 align:start size:94% position:6%
Rubio has now put forward,
which makes it simple,

00:10:33.299 --> 00:10:36.435 align:start size:84% position:16%
if Big Tech wants
Section 230 immunity,

00:10:36.435 --> 00:10:37.970
in other words, if
you're a monopoly,

00:10:37.970 --> 00:10:41.040
if you have more than 80%
market share in your space,

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.709 align:start size:97% position:3%
then you have to honor
First Amendment limitations,

00:10:43.709 --> 00:10:45.745
like Locals does voluntarily.

00:10:45.745 --> 00:10:47.880 align:start size:84% position:16%
If you honor First
Amendment limitations,

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:50.182 align:start size:84% position:16%
then you get Section
230 immunity,

00:10:50.182 --> 00:10:53.519 align:start size:97% position:3%
but if you don't honor
First Amendment limitations

00:10:53.519 --> 00:10:56.088
and you decide to censor
for political purposes,

00:10:56.088 --> 00:10:58.691
then you don't get
Section 230 immunity.

00:10:58.691 --> 00:11:00.826 align:start size:88% position:13%
That to me, that carrot
and stick approach,

00:11:00.826 --> 00:11:03.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
gets around the government
regulation problem

00:11:03.429 --> 00:11:04.930 align:start size:81% position:19%
and gets around
them getting to do

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.465
whatever they want problem.

00:11:06.465 --> 00:11:09.568
It says, "We'll give you the
carrot of special immunity,

00:11:09.568 --> 00:11:10.803
but it comes with a stick

00:11:10.803 --> 00:11:12.238 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you have to honor
the First Amendment

00:11:12.238 --> 00:11:14.240 align:start size:88% position:13%
once you acquire certain
economic influence

00:11:14.240 --> 00:11:15.307
within the marketplace."

00:11:15.307 --> 00:11:16.976
- Are you worried, though,

00:11:16.976 --> 00:11:19.211
if they got rid of
those protections,
the 230 protections,

00:11:19.211 --> 00:11:20.646
that in essence,

00:11:20.646 --> 00:11:23.482 align:start size:97% position:3%
they would have to basically
have a team of lawyers

00:11:23.482 --> 00:11:27.620
that would be watching what
everyone says all day long

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:29.822
knowing that at any given moment

00:11:29.822 --> 00:11:32.992 align:start size:97% position:3%
someone puts child pornography
on there or some other,

00:11:32.992 --> 00:11:34.293
a terrorist threat or something,

00:11:34.293 --> 00:11:35.828
that bam, (fingers snapping)

00:11:35.828 --> 00:11:37.396
they could just be sued into
oblivion and gone that day?

00:11:37.396 --> 00:11:38.698
- Yeah, that's why
I'm not in favor

00:11:38.698 --> 00:11:41.200
of just scratching
Section 230, my view,

00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm not in favor of
the government regulating.

00:11:43.002 --> 00:11:45.337
I get why people like the
idea of public utilities,

00:11:45.337 --> 00:11:47.239 align:start size:84% position:16%
et cetera, but
look at any history

00:11:47.239 --> 00:11:48.674
of the government
regulating anything

00:11:48.674 --> 00:11:50.042
and see whether that
turns out net positive.

00:11:50.042 --> 00:11:51.110
(Dave laughing)

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.411
That's why my view is give 'em,

00:11:52.411 --> 00:11:55.247
stay within the private
marketplace incentives,

00:11:55.247 --> 00:11:56.882
but just change the
incentives to say,

00:11:56.882 --> 00:11:59.452 align:start position:0%
"We're gonna give you a special
benefit nobody else gets,

00:11:59.452 --> 00:12:02.288
total immunity from suit for
anything said on your platform,

00:12:02.288 --> 00:12:04.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you just have to
honor the First Amendment

00:12:04.390 --> 00:12:06.058 align:start size:84% position:16%
and how you regulate
that platform

00:12:06.058 --> 00:12:08.294
once you have more
than 80% market share

00:12:08.294 --> 00:12:10.129 align:start size:84% position:16%
in your area of
the public square."

00:12:10.129 --> 00:12:11.931 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Do you think it's possible
that, at this point,

00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:14.867
we're like, the ship has
just sailed on all of this,

00:12:14.867 --> 00:12:18.370
that Big Tech is now
so big, so ubiquitous,

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:20.639
our government is
so dysfunctional,

00:12:20.639 --> 00:12:22.441
it's controlled by an
awful lot of people

00:12:22.441 --> 00:12:24.510
that guys like you
and I don't like,

00:12:24.510 --> 00:12:27.413 align:start size:97% position:3%
that the idea that they
could actually do anything,

00:12:27.413 --> 00:12:28.714
not only make the decision

00:12:28.714 --> 00:12:30.549
but then carry the
decision through,

00:12:30.549 --> 00:12:33.486
is just like, it's just
bananas at this point.

00:12:33.486 --> 00:12:35.154 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I think they still
have the capacity for it

00:12:35.154 --> 00:12:36.388
because they show it.

00:12:36.388 --> 00:12:38.357 align:start size:88% position:13%
The quickness with which
they got rid of Trump

00:12:38.357 --> 00:12:40.860
was a reminder that
they can invent AI

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:42.995 align:start size:84% position:16%
that's First
Amendment oriented AI

00:12:42.995 --> 00:12:44.830
to regulate their own platforms,

00:12:45.998 --> 00:12:47.633 align:start size:84% position:16%
and that's what's also
great about Locals,

00:12:47.633 --> 00:12:49.168
reason why I promote it,

00:12:49.168 --> 00:12:51.670
is Locals shows you
can have a platform

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:54.273 align:start size:84% position:16%
that is First
Amendment compliant

00:12:54.273 --> 00:12:57.309
that is technologically
capable of delivering

00:12:57.309 --> 00:13:00.146
on that First Amendment
compliant tech platform,

00:13:00.146 --> 00:13:02.715
and so if they have
problems with it,

00:13:02.715 --> 00:13:04.583 align:start size:84% position:16%
they can look to
Locals as the example

00:13:04.583 --> 00:13:06.986 align:start size:84% position:16%
and just borrow that
and implement it.

00:13:06.986 --> 00:13:08.988
They clearly have the
capacity to do it.

00:13:08.988 --> 00:13:10.489
- I gotta get you
on payroll, man,

00:13:10.489 --> 00:13:14.193
but the truth is that the way
we've dealt with it so far,

00:13:14.193 --> 00:13:16.061 align:start size:97% position:3%
first off, because you have
a paywall, as you know,

00:13:16.061 --> 00:13:18.497
just a couple of bucks,
it's as little as $2,

00:13:18.497 --> 00:13:21.667 align:start size:84% position:16%
that cleans up
99.9% of everything.

00:13:21.667 --> 00:13:23.269
We have no problem with bots

00:13:23.269 --> 00:13:25.271 align:start size:84% position:16%
and trolls and truly
hateful people.

00:13:25.271 --> 00:13:26.672
It just doesn't exist,

00:13:26.672 --> 00:13:28.174
but as I always say
to people, it's like,

00:13:28.174 --> 00:13:31.510
"Man, if you're gonna come
on and do something illegal,

00:13:31.510 --> 00:13:34.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
you got a much bigger
problem than me or Locals.

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:35.881
There's laws that exist,

00:13:35.881 --> 00:13:37.416 align:start size:97% position:3%
so you're gonna have the
government coming after you."

00:13:37.416 --> 00:13:40.052
You're not gonna worry about
what Dave Rubin's gonna do.

00:13:40.052 --> 00:13:42.588
- Precisely, and what it
shows is the capacity.

00:13:42.588 --> 00:13:44.690
Locals shows all the ability

00:13:44.690 --> 00:13:48.260 align:start position:0%
of what would a First Amendment
supporting tech platform

00:13:48.260 --> 00:13:50.062
look like without the stalking,

00:13:50.062 --> 00:13:52.431
without the harassment,
without the obscenity,

00:13:52.431 --> 00:13:54.533
without unnecessary trolling.

00:13:54.533 --> 00:13:57.002
You can have both, the
best of both worlds,

00:13:57.002 --> 00:13:58.671
and Locals proves it,

00:13:58.671 --> 00:14:01.640
and that's where I think we
can use Locals as an example,

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:04.210
not only as an exit ramp
from Big Tech monopoly

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:06.078 align:start size:84% position:16%
but also as a legal
example to say,

00:14:06.078 --> 00:14:08.547
"This is what Big Tech
should have to emulate

00:14:08.547 --> 00:14:10.816
if they want to continue
to get special immunity

00:14:10.816 --> 00:14:12.318
under the law."

00:14:12.318 --> 00:14:14.720
- I heard Alan Dershowitz
talking about this case

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:17.089 align:start position:0%
and he did say some of the
things that you just said there,

00:14:17.089 --> 00:14:19.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
that maybe it isn't
quite as tight as written

00:14:19.458 --> 00:14:20.459
as it should be,

00:14:20.459 --> 00:14:22.561
but he said that this might be

00:14:22.561 --> 00:14:25.698 align:start position:0%
the most important First
Amendment case in modern times.

00:14:25.698 --> 00:14:26.999
Do you agree with that?

00:14:26.999 --> 00:14:28.467
- Oh, I agree entirely.

00:14:28.467 --> 00:14:31.637 align:start position:0%
That's why he, I and others
want to see the suit be brought

00:14:31.637 --> 00:14:33.472
in the best, most effective way.

00:14:33.472 --> 00:14:35.274
Add claims for unjust enrichment

00:14:35.274 --> 00:14:37.977 align:start size:97% position:3%
because all these companies
got rich off of Trump,

00:14:37.977 --> 00:14:39.445
then after they got
rich off of Trump,

00:14:39.445 --> 00:14:41.347 align:start size:88% position:13%
decided they could
politically censor him.

00:14:41.347 --> 00:14:42.915
Add claims for consumer fraud

00:14:42.915 --> 00:14:44.617 align:start size:84% position:16%
because all of them
lied to people.

00:14:44.617 --> 00:14:45.885
Jack Dorsey, famously,

00:14:45.885 --> 00:14:47.920
"I'm gonna be the
free-speech wing

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.455 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the free-speech party."
(Dave laughing)

00:14:49.455 --> 00:14:52.291
I just want Jack Dorsey to
have to keep his promises,

00:14:52.291 --> 00:14:55.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the reason why I think
Dershowitz is out there

00:14:55.127 --> 00:14:57.096
is he's trying to get,

00:14:57.096 --> 00:14:59.932
with Trump, you have to talk
to him through the TV cameras,

00:14:59.932 --> 00:15:01.166
God bless him.

00:15:01.166 --> 00:15:02.668
He'll listen to
you on the phone,

00:15:02.668 --> 00:15:05.137
but he listens better when
it's through the TV camera.

00:15:05.137 --> 00:15:06.805 align:start size:84% position:16%
If Dershowitz is
giving great advice,

00:15:06.805 --> 00:15:09.975 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's absolutely one of the
most essential, critical cases

00:15:09.975 --> 00:15:11.443
for the future of the country

00:15:11.443 --> 00:15:13.579 align:start size:97% position:3%
'cause either we're gonna
have free speech or we're not,

00:15:13.579 --> 00:15:15.948 align:start size:88% position:13%
and if private companies
own the public square

00:15:15.948 --> 00:15:17.716
and it keeps going
the way it's going,

00:15:17.716 --> 00:15:19.885
free speech will
be dead in America.

00:15:19.885 --> 00:15:21.887 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Basically, you're saying
dealing with Trump as a client

00:15:21.887 --> 00:15:24.423
is completely the reverse of
how you would do it normally,

00:15:24.423 --> 00:15:26.425 align:start size:97% position:3%
where you want those
off-the-record conversations.

00:15:26.425 --> 00:15:28.394
Trump, you gotta go
on YouTube or on TV

00:15:28.394 --> 00:15:29.895
to tell him what
you're thinking.

00:15:29.895 --> 00:15:32.398
- Precisely. That's the
best way he listens.

00:15:32.398 --> 00:15:33.799
He's a unique mindset.

00:15:33.799 --> 00:15:36.468
- Yeah, so what else legally,

00:15:36.468 --> 00:15:38.671
we'll get into some of the
cultural stuff in a moment,

00:15:38.671 --> 00:15:41.540
but what else legally is
on your docket right now

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:43.809
that you're putting
your energy into?

00:15:43.809 --> 00:15:45.311
- A combination of efforts.

00:15:45.311 --> 00:15:47.680
One is in terms of the
entire election context

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:49.949 align:start size:97% position:3%
from representing the
president during the campaign,

00:15:49.949 --> 00:15:51.450
right after the campaign.

00:15:51.450 --> 00:15:53.752
There's a lot of those issues
that need to be reinforced.

00:15:53.752 --> 00:15:55.621
A lot of states are
passing good laws,

00:15:55.621 --> 00:15:57.122
helping states pass those laws,

00:15:57.122 --> 00:15:59.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
following up on the audits
that are taking place

00:15:59.291 --> 00:16:00.626 align:start size:84% position:16%
because if we don't
have confidence

00:16:00.626 --> 00:16:02.061
in our election integrity,

00:16:02.061 --> 00:16:04.163
the entire democracy
crumbles overnight.

00:16:05.331 --> 00:16:06.699
- Yeah, can you, just
real quick on that,

00:16:06.699 --> 00:16:08.801
so obviously even
talking about this,

00:16:08.801 --> 00:16:10.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
I could be blown off
YouTube in just a second,

00:16:10.302 --> 00:16:13.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
but fortunately I am on
Locals, so it's all right.

00:16:13.505 --> 00:16:15.574
What happened to all
of those lawsuits?

00:16:15.574 --> 00:16:16.875
Because there seemed to be hope.

00:16:16.875 --> 00:16:18.744
There were people that I trusted

00:16:18.744 --> 00:16:20.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
that I feel like are
sound legal minds

00:16:20.579 --> 00:16:22.414
that felt there was
some movement there

00:16:22.414 --> 00:16:25.117 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then everything
just crumbled at once.

00:16:25.117 --> 00:16:26.785
What actually happened?

00:16:26.785 --> 00:16:28.854 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I and a group of
lawyers were that close

00:16:28.854 --> 00:16:30.856
to getting to run
all the lawsuits,

00:16:30.856 --> 00:16:33.826
and our focus was
that the lawsuits

00:16:33.826 --> 00:16:35.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
were gonna be based on
the election not being run

00:16:35.728 --> 00:16:37.863
in a constitutionally
conforming manner,

00:16:37.863 --> 00:16:40.299
that there were votes
counted that were not,

00:16:40.299 --> 00:16:43.068
either by someone who is not
constitutionally qualified

00:16:43.068 --> 00:16:45.471 align:start size:84% position:16%
to vote because of age
or some other issue

00:16:45.471 --> 00:16:47.906
or because they didn't live
at the location, et cetera,

00:16:47.906 --> 00:16:50.042
or the ballot was
cast in a manner

00:16:50.042 --> 00:16:52.544 align:start size:97% position:3%
that wasn't a constitutionally
qualified manner,

00:16:53.746 --> 00:16:55.914
the signature match
check didn't conform

00:16:55.914 --> 00:16:58.050 align:start size:84% position:16%
on an absentee
ballot, as an example,

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:02.187 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the ballots were not
counted and canvassed

00:17:02.187 --> 00:17:04.323 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a constitutionally
qualified manner

00:17:04.323 --> 00:17:06.558 align:start size:97% position:3%
that conforms to international
election standards

00:17:06.558 --> 00:17:09.161 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the United States
Election Commission standards.

00:17:09.161 --> 00:17:10.763
We had established
all of these claims.

00:17:10.763 --> 00:17:13.098 align:start size:97% position:3%
We were building these suits
in all of these states.

00:17:13.098 --> 00:17:15.300
It was the ultimate
Georgia recount case

00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:16.869
that the president filed,

00:17:16.869 --> 00:17:20.639
but what happened is that it
got hijacked midway through

00:17:20.639 --> 00:17:23.842 align:start size:97% position:3%
by people who got distracted
by some shiny objects,

00:17:23.842 --> 00:17:26.812 align:start size:88% position:13%
and people who, like
Lin Wood, Sidney Powell,

00:17:26.812 --> 00:17:28.714
God bless them, Rudy Giuliani,

00:17:28.714 --> 00:17:31.417 align:start size:84% position:16%
they had no election
law background,

00:17:31.417 --> 00:17:33.519 align:start size:88% position:13%
but they felt confident
that their sources

00:17:33.519 --> 00:17:35.287 align:start size:84% position:16%
were giving them
accurate information.

00:17:35.287 --> 00:17:37.756 align:start size:97% position:3%
We were telling them, "No,
it's not accurate information.

00:17:37.756 --> 00:17:41.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a red herring that's
going to, basically,

00:17:41.393 --> 00:17:44.096
tar and feather the
legitimate claims,"

00:17:44.096 --> 00:17:45.564 align:start size:88% position:13%
and that's what
happened, unfortunately,

00:17:45.564 --> 00:17:48.233
and the president, he
knew Giuliani way back,

00:17:48.233 --> 00:17:49.835
so he was like, "Hey, this is
the guy who busted up the mob.

00:17:49.835 --> 00:17:50.803
I'll just go with that guy,"

00:17:50.803 --> 00:17:52.304
and some of us were telling him,

00:17:52.304 --> 00:17:54.673 align:start size:88% position:13%
"That's not Rudy's
thing anymore, exactly.

00:17:54.673 --> 00:17:57.142
He hasn't been in
court since 1992,"

00:17:57.142 --> 00:17:58.977
and unfortunately,
that's what happened,

00:17:58.977 --> 00:18:01.747
and so there's hearings going on

00:18:01.747 --> 00:18:03.582 align:start size:81% position:19%
about sanctions
issues, et cetera.

00:18:03.582 --> 00:18:05.884
They got distracted
by the shiny object.

00:18:05.884 --> 00:18:09.154
I always say every great
crime needs a great patsy

00:18:09.154 --> 00:18:11.924
and they fell for the great
patsy rather than looking,

00:18:11.924 --> 00:18:14.526
but that didn't mean
there was no crime.

00:18:14.526 --> 00:18:16.061
There were a lot of
constitutional issues

00:18:16.061 --> 00:18:17.563 align:start size:84% position:16%
with the election
that, unfortunately,

00:18:17.563 --> 00:18:19.731 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Supreme Court
ultimately didn't take up,

00:18:19.731 --> 00:18:22.401 align:start size:88% position:13%
I think in part because
these other claims

00:18:22.401 --> 00:18:25.104
were so outlandish that it
made a lot of judges say,

00:18:25.104 --> 00:18:26.839
"I don't want to get
anywhere near this."

00:18:26.839 --> 00:18:29.641 align:start size:88% position:13%
- In essence, if Sidney
Powell or Lin Wood

00:18:29.641 --> 00:18:32.077
or some of those guys had
not been running around

00:18:32.077 --> 00:18:33.445
with the more outlandish stuff,

00:18:33.445 --> 00:18:36.448 align:start size:97% position:3%
like Dominion voting
machines related to Venezuela

00:18:36.448 --> 00:18:37.783 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it's a plan that's
been going on for,

00:18:37.783 --> 00:18:38.984
if they had not run with that,

00:18:38.984 --> 00:18:41.687 align:start size:84% position:16%
you think that there
was enough stuff

00:18:41.687 --> 00:18:44.490 align:start size:94% position:6%
to at least get cases
that would have been heard

00:18:44.490 --> 00:18:46.992
instead of just they threw
everything out, basically.

00:18:46.992 --> 00:18:48.527
- Exactly.

00:18:48.527 --> 00:18:49.895
We were that close to getting
the Georgia Secretary of State

00:18:49.895 --> 00:18:52.197
to voluntarily give us
a whole bunch of stuff,

00:18:52.197 --> 00:18:54.833
and the moment Lin Wood
did his press conference

00:18:54.833 --> 00:18:56.301
where he said a
lotta crazy stuff

00:18:56.301 --> 00:18:58.303 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then Sidney followed
up with her stuff,

00:18:58.303 --> 00:19:00.739 align:start size:97% position:3%
he was like, "Oh, I'm not
getting anywhere near this,"

00:19:00.739 --> 00:19:03.809
that somehow the whole court
system and the legal class

00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:05.644 align:start size:84% position:16%
and even a bunch of
congressmen were like,

00:19:05.644 --> 00:19:07.779 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Okay, you're asking
me to associate

00:19:07.779 --> 00:19:09.882
with allegations of
the ghost of Chavez

00:19:09.882 --> 00:19:11.316
and China and Iran

00:19:11.316 --> 00:19:14.019
and there's secret
servers in Germany,"

00:19:14.019 --> 00:19:16.321
and I kept telling everybody
on that side of the aisle,

00:19:16.321 --> 00:19:17.756 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was like, "Even
if you believe that,

00:19:17.756 --> 00:19:19.191 align:start size:84% position:16%
no one else is going
to believe that,

00:19:19.191 --> 00:19:20.993
so let's focus on
our good claims,

00:19:20.993 --> 00:19:22.661
not get to the wild claims,"

00:19:22.661 --> 00:19:25.130
but the wild claims sucked
up all the energy in the room

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:26.598
and killed it.

00:19:26.598 --> 00:19:28.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Right, and the thing
that was so crazy about it

00:19:28.133 --> 00:19:30.169 align:start size:97% position:3%
was not just all of the
claims and everything else,

00:19:30.169 --> 00:19:31.436
but then for those of us

00:19:31.436 --> 00:19:33.038
that try to analyze
this stuff honestly,

00:19:33.038 --> 00:19:34.673
I kept saying all along, I said,

00:19:34.673 --> 00:19:38.777
"Look, if Sidney Powell, who
has a pretty good track record,

00:19:38.777 --> 00:19:41.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
if she's just
self-immolating right now,

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.182 align:start size:84% position:16%
if she's just making
crazy stuff up

00:19:43.182 --> 00:19:45.250
and gonna pour gasoline
on herself and burn up,

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:46.919
then at the end,
we'll know that,"

00:19:46.919 --> 00:19:50.455 align:start size:97% position:3%
and in a weird way, I suppose
that is what happened.

00:19:51.857 --> 00:19:53.859
Here we are. Here we are.

00:19:53.859 --> 00:19:54.927
- Exactly, but in the process,

00:19:54.927 --> 00:19:56.828
people overlooked the fact

00:19:56.828 --> 00:19:58.630 align:start size:88% position:13%
that there were a bunch
of people who voted

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:00.799
who don't appear to have
been qualified to vote,

00:20:00.799 --> 00:20:02.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what I mean by
constitutionally qualified

00:20:02.801 --> 00:20:05.504 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
is that the Constitution gives
to the state legislatures

00:20:05.504 --> 00:20:08.840 line:0%
exclusive control over
the entire voting process

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:10.342 line:0%
for the presidency,

00:20:10.342 --> 00:20:13.011 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the state legislature said
these people couldn't vote,

00:20:13.011 --> 00:20:15.214 align:start size:97% position:3%
and yet a lot of these
states allowed 'em to vote.

00:20:15.214 --> 00:20:17.015
They said they couldn't
vote by this method,

00:20:17.015 --> 00:20:19.117
and they, I'll give an example.

00:20:19.117 --> 00:20:21.653 align:start size:97% position:3%
Arizona, they just did a
small signature match check.

00:20:21.653 --> 00:20:25.023
It came back that 30 times
more signatures didn't match

00:20:25.023 --> 00:20:27.025 align:start size:84% position:16%
according to the
Democrats' own expert

00:20:27.025 --> 00:20:29.228 align:start size:84% position:16%
than was the margin
of victory in Arizona.

00:20:29.228 --> 00:20:30.963 align:start size:88% position:13%
If we had got
signature match checks,

00:20:30.963 --> 00:20:32.231
when I talked to the president,

00:20:32.231 --> 00:20:33.865
right out of the gate I said,

00:20:33.865 --> 00:20:35.934
"If they'll give you
signature match checks,

00:20:35.934 --> 00:20:37.669
the election is
on the up and up.

00:20:37.669 --> 00:20:39.204
If they won't,

00:20:39.204 --> 00:20:41.707
that means they're scared
that there's problems."

00:20:41.707 --> 00:20:44.543 align:start position:0%
No state would allow a
signature match check to occur.

00:20:44.543 --> 00:20:46.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
- What was their argument
for not allowing you?

00:20:46.378 --> 00:20:47.646
Was it simply just like,

00:20:47.646 --> 00:20:49.681
"We're the Democrats and
we got what we wanted,

00:20:49.681 --> 00:20:51.149
so (laughing)"?

00:20:51.149 --> 00:20:52.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Originally, they didn't
have good arguments

00:20:52.718 --> 00:20:56.154
and then their arguments became
Sidney Powell's allegations.

00:20:56.154 --> 00:20:58.824
They're like, "We're not gonna
dignify these crazy claims,"

00:20:58.824 --> 00:21:00.392
and so forth.

00:21:00.392 --> 00:21:02.494
They used that as their best
cover, their best fig leaf,

00:21:02.494 --> 00:21:03.962
because I'll give an example.

00:21:03.962 --> 00:21:06.698 align:start size:97% position:3%
The Georgia Secretary of
State promised back in 2018,

00:21:06.698 --> 00:21:08.233
when he digitized
all the ballots

00:21:08.233 --> 00:21:09.801 align:start size:84% position:16%
with the contract with
Dominion, he said,

00:21:09.801 --> 00:21:11.236
"What's great about this

00:21:11.236 --> 00:21:13.438 align:start size:94% position:6%
is we'll now print ballots
to the entire world.

00:21:13.438 --> 00:21:16.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can publish every
ballot to the whole world

00:21:16.074 --> 00:21:17.909
and everybody can see how
clean the election is."

00:21:17.909 --> 00:21:19.645
One of the first
things I asked him

00:21:19.645 --> 00:21:21.280
when I came down for
the president was,

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:22.514
"Why don't, so let's
go ahead and do that,"

00:21:22.514 --> 00:21:24.316
and he's like, "I'll
get back to that."

00:21:24.316 --> 00:21:25.817
He never got around to it,

00:21:25.817 --> 00:21:27.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
which means there's
something in those ballots

00:21:27.819 --> 00:21:29.054
that's unusual.

00:21:29.054 --> 00:21:30.055
There's something
in those ballots

00:21:30.055 --> 00:21:30.989
that will lead people to say,

00:21:30.989 --> 00:21:32.557
"Hmm, why does it look that way?

00:21:32.557 --> 00:21:34.426
Why does it have this problem?"

00:21:34.426 --> 00:21:35.994 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I can already tell
you what some of them are.

00:21:35.994 --> 00:21:37.863
Some of them, from
the ballots we saw,

00:21:37.863 --> 00:21:39.798
there were people who
were writing in names

00:21:39.798 --> 00:21:43.001 align:start size:97% position:3%
and signing in ways that were
completely contradictory.

00:21:43.001 --> 00:21:44.269
You could look at him and say,

00:21:44.269 --> 00:21:46.738 align:start size:84% position:16%
"That's probably not
the same person,"

00:21:46.738 --> 00:21:50.008 align:start position:0%
and unfortunately, those really
good claims got swamped out

00:21:50.008 --> 00:21:51.343
by the bad claims.

00:21:51.343 --> 00:21:53.378 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Do you think that
the states like Arizona

00:21:53.378 --> 00:21:54.846
that's doing some
audit stuff now

00:21:54.846 --> 00:21:57.282 align:start size:88% position:13%
and Georgia now is
trying to pass some laws

00:21:57.282 --> 00:21:59.685 align:start size:84% position:16%
that everyone of
course is saying are
racist and everything,

00:21:59.685 --> 00:22:03.955 align:start position:0%
are any of these laws to
tighten up the roles, show IDs,

00:22:03.955 --> 00:22:07.292 align:start position:0%
basic things that are being
called tools of white supremacy,

00:22:07.292 --> 00:22:09.127
you think this stuff can work?

00:22:09.127 --> 00:22:09.961
- Oh, absolutely.

00:22:11.396 --> 00:22:14.499
We've identified a wide range
of weaknesses in the system

00:22:14.499 --> 00:22:16.935
that were exploited in 2020

00:22:16.935 --> 00:22:18.337
that are now getting corrected

00:22:18.337 --> 00:22:19.771
in most states in the country.

00:22:19.771 --> 00:22:21.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not all states, California
is going more crazy,

00:22:21.807 --> 00:22:24.376
but every place else,
for the most part,

00:22:24.376 --> 00:22:25.911 align:start size:84% position:16%
is actually tightening
down the laws,

00:22:25.911 --> 00:22:27.546
especially in these
key swing states.

00:22:27.546 --> 00:22:29.681 align:start size:97% position:3%
Wisconsin acknowledged that
they're not gonna allow

00:22:29.681 --> 00:22:31.249
that same thing to happen again.

00:22:31.249 --> 00:22:33.185 align:start size:97% position:3%
Michigan is saying they're not
gonna allow the same thing.

00:22:33.185 --> 00:22:34.353
Georgia. Arizona.

00:22:34.353 --> 00:22:35.921 align:start size:84% position:16%
Pennsylvania is
about to do an audit,

00:22:35.921 --> 00:22:37.522
and I am for all audits.

00:22:37.522 --> 00:22:39.224
It's what I tell my
friends on the left.

00:22:39.224 --> 00:22:40.692
We should always have audits

00:22:40.692 --> 00:22:42.994
so everybody has confidence
in the election outcome.

00:22:42.994 --> 00:22:44.663
This isn't about right or left.

00:22:44.663 --> 00:22:46.264
This is about having confidence

00:22:46.264 --> 00:22:48.133
that the election was
done on the up and up,

00:22:48.133 --> 00:22:50.902 align:start size:97% position:3%
and what better way to do
so than a transparent audit?

00:22:52.304 --> 00:22:53.438
What I tell people throughout

00:22:53.438 --> 00:22:54.639
was when the state kept saying,

00:22:54.639 --> 00:22:56.208 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Don't worry,
everything's fine,"

00:22:56.208 --> 00:22:57.843 align:start size:81% position:19%
that's like asking
Bernie Madoff,

00:22:57.843 --> 00:22:59.344 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Have you taken a
look at your books?"

00:22:59.344 --> 00:23:00.278
and Bernie came back and said,

00:23:00.278 --> 00:23:01.713
"Yeah, my books are still good."

00:23:01.713 --> 00:23:03.515 align:start size:97% position:3%
(Dave laughing)
That's not the way we do it.

00:23:03.515 --> 00:23:05.584
We give an audit and that's
the way we should do it.

00:23:05.584 --> 00:23:07.419
- You mean you don't let
the guy audit himself?

00:23:07.419 --> 00:23:08.286
That's not how it works?

00:23:08.286 --> 00:23:09.688
- Precisely.

00:23:09.688 --> 00:23:11.923 align:start position:0%
You don't let the people
accused of doing something wrong

00:23:11.923 --> 00:23:13.392 align:start size:84% position:16%
be the ones to tell
you, "No, don't worry.

00:23:13.392 --> 00:23:14.893
Everything's cool."

00:23:14.893 --> 00:23:16.895
- How is this, what we're
talking about right now,

00:23:16.895 --> 00:23:18.964
directly related to
the Trump lawsuit?

00:23:18.964 --> 00:23:20.999
Because obviously, as you know,

00:23:20.999 --> 00:23:23.668
there's a slight chance that
YouTube won't let us post this

00:23:23.668 --> 00:23:25.537
that you're saying right now.

00:23:25.537 --> 00:23:27.572
We know that that
is a possibility.

00:23:27.572 --> 00:23:30.742 align:start size:97% position:3%
That could be directly related
to Trump's lawsuit, right?

00:23:30.742 --> 00:23:32.010
- Absolutely, and one of the,

00:23:32.010 --> 00:23:33.845
what a bunch of us are
telling Trump's team

00:23:33.845 --> 00:23:35.380
to add to the lawsuit

00:23:35.380 --> 00:23:38.316
is to add two components
on the election aspect.

00:23:38.316 --> 00:23:40.819
One is add all the
Hunter Biden stuff,

00:23:40.819 --> 00:23:42.587
all the suppression
of Hunter Biden.

00:23:42.587 --> 00:23:44.423
That was Big Tech censorship

00:23:44.423 --> 00:23:46.625
at the request of
a political party

00:23:46.625 --> 00:23:49.227
and arguably state actors.

00:23:49.227 --> 00:23:50.729
I think they'll find proof.

00:23:50.729 --> 00:23:52.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Right, that one seems
like the more obvious one,

00:23:52.130 --> 00:23:53.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
that clearly they couldn't
have just decided,

00:23:53.832 --> 00:23:55.100
everyone at once, no,

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:56.868
you can't talk about the laptop

00:23:56.868 --> 00:23:58.703 align:start size:88% position:13%
and we're not gonna
let the "New York Post"

00:23:58.703 --> 00:24:00.405
print journalism.

00:24:00.405 --> 00:24:03.241 align:start position:0%
- Arguably, the biggest coverup
of a presidential election

00:24:03.241 --> 00:24:05.877 align:start size:84% position:16%
political scandal
in American history,

00:24:05.877 --> 00:24:07.946
and so I would've included that.

00:24:07.946 --> 00:24:09.414
I would've included
it as a lot of this

00:24:09.414 --> 00:24:12.317 align:start size:97% position:3%
were really illicit in-kind
campaign contributions.

00:24:12.317 --> 00:24:14.286 align:start size:84% position:16%
Then you tie in
the election aspect

00:24:14.286 --> 00:24:16.788
because a lot of these
election rule changes

00:24:16.788 --> 00:24:19.157
were being funded
by Mark Zuckerberg.

00:24:19.157 --> 00:24:24.162 align:start position:0%
He was privately financing
various clerks, election clerks,

00:24:25.297 --> 00:24:26.965 align:start size:88% position:13%
to change the rules
throughout the country.

00:24:26.965 --> 00:24:28.700
Why not add that to the lawsuit?

00:24:28.700 --> 00:24:30.435 align:start size:84% position:16%
Because then you
have a robust lawsuit

00:24:30.435 --> 00:24:32.237
that gets to all
of these scandals,

00:24:32.237 --> 00:24:34.706
that entitles you to a
wider range of discovery,

00:24:34.706 --> 00:24:37.142
gives you a better argument to
get past motions to dismiss,

00:24:37.142 --> 00:24:39.144
and I think the president
would be legally entitled

00:24:39.144 --> 00:24:40.745
to bring all of them.

00:24:40.745 --> 00:24:43.415 align:start size:84% position:16%
- He's personally
suing these guys too?

00:24:43.415 --> 00:24:45.083
He's personally
suing Zuckerberg?

00:24:45.083 --> 00:24:47.619
How does that even
become part of this?

00:24:47.619 --> 00:24:48.854
- What could have been the suit.

00:24:48.854 --> 00:24:50.388
Right now, the way it's drafted,

00:24:50.388 --> 00:24:53.225 align:start size:97% position:3%
it's highly likely that those
claims will be dismissed.

00:24:53.225 --> 00:24:54.993
I think what Trump
was thinking about,

00:24:54.993 --> 00:24:57.963 align:start position:0%
where they could amend the
complaint to properly allege it,

00:24:57.963 --> 00:24:59.431
is that the way he saw this

00:24:59.431 --> 00:25:02.467 align:start size:97% position:3%
is this didn't go from state
actor direct to Big Tech

00:25:02.467 --> 00:25:04.035
and then to Zuckerberg,

00:25:04.035 --> 00:25:08.874
it went from state actor
to Zuckerberg to Facebook.

00:25:08.874 --> 00:25:11.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's not suing Zuckerberg,
if he does it right,

00:25:11.243 --> 00:25:14.212 align:start size:97% position:3%
he's not suing Zuckerberg
because of what Facebook did

00:25:14.212 --> 00:25:16.481
for which Zuckerberg could
not be individually sued

00:25:16.481 --> 00:25:17.916
under the corporate veil,

00:25:17.916 --> 00:25:20.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
but he's suing him because
Zuckerberg was using

00:25:20.151 --> 00:25:23.522
his power over Facebook at
the request of the state

00:25:23.522 --> 00:25:25.323
to control the public dialogue

00:25:25.323 --> 00:25:27.792 align:start size:94% position:6%
and manipulate the
outcomes of the election.

00:25:27.792 --> 00:25:29.761 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Is part of the problem
here that we know

00:25:29.761 --> 00:25:32.797 align:start size:97% position:3%
that people can lie to
Congress and nothing happens?

00:25:32.797 --> 00:25:35.800 align:start position:0%
The famous James Clapper
scratching the top of his head,

00:25:35.800 --> 00:25:38.503
"We do not wittingly spy
on the American people,"

00:25:38.503 --> 00:25:41.406
flat out lie and now
he's a CNN contributor,

00:25:41.406 --> 00:25:43.408
or Jack Dorsey at Twitter

00:25:43.408 --> 00:25:46.711 align:start size:97% position:3%
basically telling Ted Cruz,
"We don't shadow ban,"

00:25:46.711 --> 00:25:49.214
and it's like, you obviously do,

00:25:49.214 --> 00:25:51.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
but of course, I know with
a word like shadow ban,

00:25:51.249 --> 00:25:53.385 align:start size:84% position:16%
it doesn't have a
technical definition,

00:25:53.385 --> 00:25:55.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
so he can probably wiggle
out of it that way,

00:25:55.353 --> 00:25:58.290
but the point is that you
can lie to Congress now

00:25:58.290 --> 00:25:59.991
and it just doesn't matter.

00:25:59.991 --> 00:26:02.027
- Yeah, unless you're
Roger Stone, (laughing)

00:26:02.027 --> 00:26:03.828 align:start size:84% position:16%
unless you're the
wrong political party,

00:26:03.828 --> 00:26:06.965 align:start size:97% position:3%
then maybe the law will matter
suddenly, but absolutely,

00:26:06.965 --> 00:26:11.102 align:start size:97% position:3%
that's the bifurcated,
two-tiered system of justice

00:26:11.102 --> 00:26:13.438
that the Department of
Justice has accelerated

00:26:13.438 --> 00:26:17.309 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the Trump era is one of
the greatest risks and threats

00:26:17.309 --> 00:26:19.477
to justice and its integrity

00:26:19.477 --> 00:26:21.313
and the perception
of its integrity

00:26:21.313 --> 00:26:22.814
amongst the broader public.

00:26:22.814 --> 00:26:24.349
- Yeah. All right.

00:26:24.349 --> 00:26:26.651
Election, Trump, okay.

00:26:26.651 --> 00:26:28.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe my YouTube
